<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4905" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμάντευτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not to be foretold</i> or
				<i>conjectured,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύχη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Max.Tyr.
					11.6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>lacking in oracles,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not divining,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ μέλλοντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Charito
					2.2
				</span></i>
			: hence, of dogs with bad noses, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				5.63
			</span></i>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμαντις</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span></b> , <i>not divining,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. μαντική</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Oenom.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				5.21
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
